                <pb facs="0678" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/803: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-13T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 13—11:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. My No. 1, January 3, 2 p.m. I am informed by Ginman that the Chinese are now
                    pressing him very urgently for action. It is suggested that a decision be
                    expedited as much as possible in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
